+- Chakravarti (Mathematics of Operations Research 1989) is verified. It treats isotonic median regression via linear programming and is useful only as an analogy for deriving pooling/PAVA-like algorithms from LP duals.
+- Federgruen and Groenevelt (Operations Research 1986) is verified. It studies greedy optimality for resource-allocation problems with nested/group constraints; relevant as a possible proof-technology analogy for front-loaded low-mass allocation, not direct support for the drought formula.
 
