+\]
+with \(h=1\) has reduced-LP value \(68/225\approx0.3022\), whereas the naive last-low-only expression gives \(1.8(1-0.9)=0.18\). The earlier \(0.4\)-horizon genuinely binds. This is not yet promoted as a full \(D_n\) theorem until the unequal-low full-to-reduced LP proof is written, but it is a decisive regression test against any simple last-low formula for variable low levels.
